      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://easttennesseecrossingbyway.com/%F0%9F%8C%B2-the-story-of-white-pine-tennessee-from-dandridge-crossing-to-a-scenic-byway-town/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town adopted the name White Pine in 1873 after a large pine tree that once stood on Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pine%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the Civil War, a railroad line was built through the area, turning the community into a bustling rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pine%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "White Pine lies along the East Tennessee Crossing National Scenic Byway, a federally recognized 83‑mile route through the Appalachians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
